      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butler%2C_Alabama"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Founded in 1848, Butler became Choctaw County’s seat the year the county was created in 1847.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butler%2C_Alabama"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Alabama, Tennessee and Northern Railroad reached Butler in 1912, spurring growth and connecting the town to regional trade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/butler/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Butler’s historic courthouse and the nearby Zack Rogers House are listed on the Alabama Register of Landmarks and Heritage.",
